    "note_tweet": {
      "entities": {},
      "text": "I think what people often seem to forget is that womanhood and manhood are asymmetrical categories: womanhood is a situation that one often inadvertently falls into while manhood is an aspiration that one needs to actively pursue. In this sense, trans women are feminized through their exclusion from and refusal of manhood; trans men become men by rejecting their denigration into womanhood. The inaccessibility of manhood (as absence) thus forms the condition of the former while the inevitability of womanhood (as presence) can still provide grounding for the latter."
